Create a new Chinese-style fine-line colored decorative illustration poster based on classical poetry, transforming the scenery, actions, and emotions in the poem into an Oriental scene with a clear visual narrative.

Use a high-angle overhead view, Oriental scattered perspective, and modern graphic composition. Tree crowns are soft and fluffy cloud-like color blocks, with edges having a fine powder-stippled texture, interspersed with slender continuous ink-black branches. Buildings use fine Gongbi line drawing, blue-green tiles, warm white walls, and vermilion wooden structures.

Figures, animals, and plants use unified fine line drawing and flat coloring, with natural actions, accurate structures, and clear spatial relationships between subjects.

The ground and water surfaces are represented by large areas of warm off-white blank space, supplemented by a small amount of ink shadows and simple thin lines. The composition changes flexibly according to the poem, highlighting core imagery and maintaining clear primary and secondary order and organized density.

Colors use Oriental traditional color systems such as azurite, mineral green, indigo, cinnabar, ochre red, and ivory white. The coloring is full and even, matte and clean, retaining a slight paper texture.

Add large warm white Chinese titles, small vertical rows of the original poem lines, author signatures, and a few red seals to form a complete Oriental cultural art poster.

Avoid realistic photography, 3D, anime, heavy ink wash, oil painting impasto, complex backgrounds, excessive grain, and artificial aging.

The final presentation has a textbook-level fine illustration texture, combining Oriental aesthetics, poetic blank space, and vivid visual narrative.

