Create a New Chinese-style fine-line colored decorative illustration poster based on ancient poetry, transforming the scenery, space, and emotions in the poem into a complete Eastern poetic scene.

Use high-angle bird's-eye view, Eastern scattered perspective, and modern flat composition. Tree canopies appear as soft, fluffy cloud-like color blocks with a delicate powder-dotted texture, interspersed with slender, continuous ink-black branches. Traditional buildings use fine Gongbi line drawing, regular malachite green tiles, white walls, and vermilion pillars. Ground and water surfaces use large areas of warm off-white negative space, paired with a small number of irregular ink-black shadows.

The color scheme uses full, clean, and matte traditional Eastern color palettes, with the main color forming visual weight, supplemented by colors such as azurite, malachite green, cinnabar, and ochre red, maintaining a delicate and unified paper-based decorative illustration texture.

The image highlights core imagery, establishing visual layers through natural curves, color block encirclement, and density contrasts. The composition changes with the content of the poetry, without forcibly adding unrelated buildings or trees.

Incorporate a large warm-white Chinese title, small vertically arranged poem lines, author signature, and a few vermilion seals to form a complete ancient poetry art poster.

Avoid realistic landscapes, heavy ink wash, 3D, oil painting, anime style, complex distant views, excessive grain, and artificial aging. Maintain textbook-level fine lines, soft coloring, and Eastern decorative aesthetics.

