使用具有触感的纯手工纸、大面积色块、结构化构图和微型叙事场景，创作一张精致的竖版文化海报。

以清晰的纸质构造方法构建主要视觉效果。构图可以使用分层孔径、取景框、重叠的印刷色块、折叠平面或其他物理纸张关系。让结构本身创造深度、节奏和视觉张力，而不是依赖装饰性图形。

所有大面积纸张区域都应具有真实的手工质感，包括可见的纤维、纸浆变化、颜料吸收、细微的压力痕迹、不规则边缘和轻微的材质瑕疵。保持表面哑光、干净且高级。

使用强烈但受控的色彩关系。大面积色块从远处看应保持视觉清晰，而较小的重叠、切割边缘、阴影、折痕和纸张厚度只有在近距离观察时才可见。

添加一个与主题相关的小型微缩场景。包括两到三名成年人自然地进行活动，例如剪纸、操作压榨机、表演皮影戏、折叠结构或排列材料。保持整个场景占海报的 3% 到 5% 左右，使其成为一个被发现的细节，而不是主体。

使用大量的暖象牙色或中性负空间来平衡巨大的结构形状。

排版应克制且处于次要地位。主标题使用精致的编辑级衬线体，辅助信息使用小型大写无衬线体。标题应相对较小，并放置在构图中安静的区域。

视觉阅读顺序应为：

首先是大面积纸张结构，其次是色彩与材质的相互作用，第三是微缩场景，最后是标题和活动信息。

最终效果应具有现代感、触感、编辑感、建筑感和手工感。从远处看，海报应被视为一个强有力的抽象构图。近距离观察时，它应展现出纸张纤维、切割边缘、折痕、重叠、印刷纹理、微型人物、工具和过程。

Please make the photo I uploaded into a 3:4 vertical "Original Photography at the top / Line Art Translation at the bottom" comparison poster.

**[Keep the Subject Realistic]**

The people in the photo always maintain a complete photo-level realistic effect. Facial features, skin tone, hairstyle, hair color, expressions, movements, clothing, accessories, and body proportions are all taken from the original photo—do not redraw, do not change clothes, do not change movements, do not add or subtract people, and do not have missing limbs.

The image continues to use the original photo's framing, cropping range, lens angle, person size, and location—do not mirror, do not re-center, do not scale randomly, and do not create new movements for the person. The person always stays in their original position as the real visual subject of the image. Important objects the person is holding or using can continue to retain the photo texture.

**[Convert Environment into Hand-drawn World]**

In the bottom half, the environment around the person completely breaks away from the photographic texture and shifts to a soft warm-white paper background.

Buildings, trees, mountains, walls, doors/windows, curtains, furniture, books, plants, lamps, carpets, photo frames, and other background objects are all simplified based on the position and proportions of the original photo, redrawn with loose, generalized monochromatic lines.

There is no need to copy all real details; only keep the main outlines, size relationships, and spatial positions that allow the scene to be identified. Remove the original background colors, real shadows, photographic textures, and material expressions.

**[Monochromatic Line Rules]**

The entire environment in the bottom half only allows the use of **one saturated monochromatic ink line**.

Prioritize extracting an obvious non-neutral color from the original photo, then adjust it to a clear, bright, medium-saturation color. If the original image is generally grey, white, or has no obvious primary color, automatically choose an accent color that coordinates with the image, such as cobalt blue, brick red, coral red, forest green, deep cyan, purple, wine red, ochre orange, etc.

One image can only have one line art color; mixing a second color is not allowed.

The line texture should not be like a fine pen drawing, nor like a pencil sketch, but closer to the **casual drawing feel between a medium marker and a ballpoint pen**: lines can shake slightly, thickness and pressure can vary slightly, turns do not have to be perfectly accurate, connections can be slightly misaligned, and line ends are allowed to slightly overshoot, giving an overall natural feel of being drawn in one go.

Outlines should not be too neat; they should retain a bit of clumsiness, imperfection, and spontaneity.

Objects should be summarized with simple shapes as much as possible:

Books are represented by simple rectangles;

Plants are represented by several groups of loose leaves;

Lamps are represented by simple domes and supports;

Windows only keep the basic frame;

Fabric only has a few sparse folds drawn.

Do not strive to fill the whole drawing; retain a large amount of warm-white negative space to make the image relaxed, breathable, and have a bit of an unfinished manuscript feel.

**[Ground and Space Treatment]**

The ground, roads, tabletops, wall corners, countertops, etc., only keep the most basic outer outlines and a few structural seam lines.

Do not use a grey base, do not draw real shadows, do not fill large areas with color, and do not create 3D light and shadow. All environmental elements always use the same ink color, letting the photo-realistic person naturally overlap on top of the monochromatic hand-drawn environment.

**[Overall Visual Direction]**

The final effect should present a clear **"Realistic Subject × Coarse Monochromatic Hand-drawn Environment"** contrast.

Overall temperament leanings:

**Editorial collage, independent magazine lifestyle illustration, simple environmental graffiti, clean warm-white paper, minimalist, interesting, relaxed.**

The bottom half is not a refined illustration, but a generalized monochromatic background manuscript with human traces.

**[Prohibited]**

Do not draw real people as illustrations or cartoons;

Do not change the person's identity, face, clothing, and posture;

Do not add extra people;

Do not have missing hands/feet or limb errors;

Do not add important objects out of thin air that do not exist in the original image;

Do not use multi-color line art;

Do not retain realistic photographic backgrounds;

Do not do gradients, watercolors, 3D, anime, manga, or refined vector illustrations;

Do not add text, logos, watermarks, interface elements, or any UI.

